    "durationMs": 127240,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete. Built the URL Shortener API from scratch in /workspace with:\n\n- **`app/`** — FastAPI app: `POST /links` (201, generated or custom codes, 409 on duplicates), `GET /links/{code}` (404 JSON errors), `GET /r/{code}` (302 with atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING` click increment, exactly once per request), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `items`/`total`). Custom exception handlers make all 404/409/422 responses return an `error` field, including FastAPI's default validation errors for malformed JSON.\n- **Validation** — URLs must parse as absolute http/https with a host and are returned byte-for-byte unchanged (no Pydantic URL normalization); codes match `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`.\n- **Persistence** — SQLAlchemy 2.0 + psycopg3, `DATABASE_URL` read via pydantic-settings (no hard-coded credentials), Alembic migration creating the `links` table, re-runs idempotently on start.\n- **`start.sh`** — applies `alembic upgrade head` then serves uvicorn on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground.\n\nVerified end-to-end: 25 pytest cases pass (including malformed JSON, boundary code lengths, URL-unchanged checks), and after killing and restarting the server, links and click counts survived and kept incrementing. Test server is stopped and the port is free."
  }
